# Examples

Six programs made to be shown in a slide, to start from the one closest to yours. They go from basic to
advanced graphics, and each one uses another interface: none, the mouse, a panel, buttons in the slide,
ImGui, a value sent back to the slide. Each one is a folder of [the repository]({{ repo }}/tree/main/examples):
its sources, a built copy for the web (`web/`, to use as it is), its poster for the PDF, its browser test,
and a README with the settings of its address.

## Two example talks

The same demos in two slide tools: nothing in the demos depends on the tool.

- [In lhtml-site](../../decks/lhtml-site/html/index.html), five slides, and [their PDF](../../decks/lhtml-site/slides.pdf)
  where each demo is replaced by its poster.
- [In reveal.js](../../decks/reveal.js/index.html), four slides: plain `<iframe>`s, and buttons that name their
  demo (`data-demo="#surface"`).

